{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJBSRd37fjnZGXbPsLu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `saveAll` in `store.js`. The existing test passes, but I didn't add a test that reproduces the early-resolve bug.\n\nThe cause was `items.forEach(async ...)`. `forEach` ignores the promises its callback returns, so `saveAll` returned `items.length` before any `db.put` had finished. A failed write also became an unhandled rejection instead of making `saveAll` reject.\n\nIt now does `await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)))`. `saveAll` resolves with the count only after every write finishes. If any write fails, it rejects, as the comment at the top of the file says.\n\nThe writes now all start at once, as they did before. If `db` needs limited concurrency or ordered writes, a sequential `for...of` loop would do that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":22807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561},"output_tokens":259,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9334737-c18f-41b3-8d21-791d808d01ae","uuid":"79466ac3-6c87-4985-9722-9262473f7db8","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:23:55.544Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJBSGwYGuPRHv98T67V"}
